From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 04:57:39 -0647
Subject: [PATCH] nfc: nci: don't log unhandled proprietary notifications as
 errors

A notification in the proprietary group (GID 0xF) that the driver has
no handler for is the controller vendor's own and is dropped anyway, but
nci_ntf_packet() logs each one with pr_err(). Some controllers send them
continuously: the ST54L on the Pixel 9a, driven by nxp-nci as a plain NCI
controller, sends opcode 0xf02 on every discovery cycle, about 14 times a
second while polling, so the kernel log filled with

  nci: nci_ntf_packet: unsupported ntf opcode 0xf02

Log them at debug level instead. Unknown notifications outside the
proprietary group still go through the switch below.

Signed-off-by: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 net/nfc/nci/ntf.c | 12 ++++++++----
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/net/nfc/nci/ntf.c b/net/nfc/nci/ntf.c
index f5c9a8ab7..e2758152d 100644
--- a/net/nfc/nci/ntf.c
+++ b/net/nfc/nci/ntf.c
@@ -1001,10 +1001,14 @@ void nci_ntf_packet(struct nci_dev *ndev, struct sk_buff *skb)
 	skb_pull(skb, NCI_CTRL_HDR_SIZE);
 
 	if (nci_opcode_gid(ntf_opcode) == NCI_GID_PROPRIETARY) {
-		if (nci_prop_ntf_packet(ndev, ntf_opcode, skb) == -ENOTSUPP) {
-			pr_err("unsupported ntf opcode 0x%x\n",
-			       ntf_opcode);
-		}
+		/*
+		 * Proprietary notifications are the controller vendor's own:
+		 * one the driver has no handler for is ignored, not an error.
+		 * Some controllers send them on every discovery cycle.
+		 */
+		if (nci_prop_ntf_packet(ndev, ntf_opcode, skb) == -ENOTSUPP)
+			pr_debug("unhandled proprietary ntf opcode 0x%x\n",
+				 ntf_opcode);
 
 		goto end;
 	}
